course: dictionary
lesson: 15237
title: Shattered: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Shattered can mean broken into many small pieces, extremely tired, or very shocked and upset. The words around it show you which meaning fits.
explain: «The vase fell off the shelf and shattered on the floor.» A vase can break into tiny pieces, but it cannot be tired or upset. The clues say the vase broke, so shattered means broken into many small pieces.
explain: «After sports day, Ella said, "I'm absolutely shattered!" and fell asleep on the sofa.» Ella is not broken. She is very tired, and falling asleep is the clue. Check by putting your meaning into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Shattered is an adjective, and it is also the past form of the verb shatter.
fact: «Shattered» means broken into many small pieces, as in «shattered glass».
fact: In everyday British, Australian and New Zealand talk, «shattered» (informal) means extremely tired.
fact: «Shattered» can also mean very shocked and upset, as in «shattered dreams».
fact: To choose the right meaning, look at the words around it: a glass, a sports day, or a dream tells you which meaning fits.
exercise: «The window shattered when the ball hit it.» What does shattered mean here? | Painted bright red | Extremely tired | *Broken into many small pieces | Very happy
exercise: Sam says, «I'm shattered after the football match.» What does shattered mean in this talk? | Very shocked | *Extremely tired | Cold and wet | Broken into small pieces
exercise: «When the team lost the final, his dreams were shattered.» Which meaning fits here? | Extremely tired after a long run | Broken into many small pieces | Shiny and bright | *Very shocked and upset
test: «He dropped his phone and the screen shattered.» Which meaning fits best? | *Broken into many small pieces | Extremely tired | Very happy | Lost in the woods
test: Ava says, «I'm shattered, can we sit down?» What does she mean? | She is glad to be home | She has broken something | She is very shocked | *She is extremely tired
exam: «The news was so upsetting that Mia was shattered, and she could not speak for an hour.» Which meaning fits best here? | *Very shocked and upset | Extremely tired | Shiny and bright | Broken into many small pieces
